Just one: **plan_ExchangeRate**.

Verified from TM1: its rule contains a `DB('plan_Control','Corporate Currency','Setting')` reference —

```
skipcheck;

['local']=1;

[]=IF(!plan_currency @= DB('plan_Control','Corporate Currency','Setting'),1, STET);
```

No other cube's rules reference plan_Control, and plan_Control's own rules don't read any cube. No TI processes were found writing to or reading from it either.

Unknown: the live scan can't see processes that reference the cube only through a variable name, or that read it purely via a cube-view datasource. Running a metadata extraction would let me check those in graph mode.

Side note while I was in the rule: plan_ExchangeRate uses `SKIPCHECK` with no `FEEDERS` section, which is a common cause of consolidated totals reading zero. Happy to run a rule analysis on it if you want that looked at.
